  "notes": "Cash basis county; governmental only. Basic statement receipts/disbursements from the Total Governmental Funds column (p4); Taxes 4,035,652 split into property/motor vehicle/lodging/other using the statement of activities general receipts (p2), which sum exactly. Local receipts (2,207,460) kept as one broad line. Balance sheet from the Statement of Net Position - Cash Basis (p1). Transfers in and out both 3,649,853 (net zero). Detail: General Fund recorded from the budget schedule (p11, by department, more detailed than the p5 General Fund column of the combining statement, which is not recorded to avoid double counting); the p11 General Fund budget schedule excludes the Inheritance Tax Fund, so that fund (part of the General Fund, printed only in the p5 combining statement Inheritance Tax Fund column) is recorded separately in detail as fund Inheritance Tax (revenue 640,237; disbursements 760,498 by function; transfers out 503,241), which is not a double count. Detail transfers in (3,649,853) now net against transfers out (3,649,853). Road, Flowage Easement and Employee Health Benefits from budget schedules (p12-14); nonmajor funds via Total Nonmajor column (p10, more than 6 funds); p6-9 per-fund nonmajor columns not recorded. Budget column for GF and others is Final (or Original/Final). Read pages 1-14 of 14"
